<BaseLayout title="Owner maintenance checks">
  <h1>Owner maintenance checks</h1>
  <p>This page is a between-service inspection checklist, not a replacement for scheduled maintenance. Use the owner's manual for safe checking procedures and the VIN-specific service schedule for workshop operations.</p>

  <h2>At each fuel stop</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Check engine-oil level using the method and conditions described in the owner's manual.</li>
    <li>Clean the windshield and inspect wiper blades, washer operation, headlights, and taillights.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Monthly</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Check cold tire pressures with a reliable gauge and compare them with the driver's-door/B-pillar placard.</li>
    <li>Inspect tire tread and sidewalls for uneven wear, cuts, bulges, cracking, or embedded objects.</li>
    <li>Check accessible coolant and other fluid levels against their marked limits, following the manual's warnings.</li>
    <li>Look for fresh fluid spots beneath the parked vehicle and visible leaks in the engine compartment.</li>
    <li>Visually inspect battery terminals for corrosion or loose connections. Do not disconnect the battery without following Volvo's procedure.</li>
    <li>Check exterior lighting and confirm wipers and washers operate correctly.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Seasonally and before long trips</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Recheck tire pressures as ambient temperatures change.</li>
    <li>Inspect tire tread, spare or tire-repair equipment, lights, wipers, and washer-fluid freeze protection.</li>
    <li>Wash the underbody after exposure to road salt, where practical.</li>
    <li>Clear leaves and debris from the air-intake/cowl area at the base of the windshield.</li>
    <li>Check that the maintenance record is current and that no service reminder or warning message is being ignored.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Stop and arrange service if</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>A red warning directs you to stop, or oil pressure, engine temperature, or braking is abnormal.</li>
    <li>You find a brake-fluid, fuel, coolant, or significant oil leak.</li>
    <li>A tire has a bulge, exposed cord, sidewall damage, or rapidly falling pressure.</li>
    <li>Steering, braking, wheel vibration, or drivetrain behavior changes suddenly.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Record the checks</h2>
  <p>Record the date, odometer, tire pressures, fluid observations, visible defects, and any action taken. A recurring change is often more useful diagnostically than a single observation.</p>

  <h2>Source</h2>
  <p><a href="https://www.volvocars.com/us/support/car/s60/20w46">Volvo Cars — 2021 S60 owner's information</a>. The maintenance schedule and vehicle-specific instructions take precedence over this summary.</p>
  <h2>What an inspection may cost in 2026</h2>
  <p>Owner-performed checks above are free apart from basic supplies. If you ask a shop to diagnose a concern or perform a dedicated brake inspection, budget approximately <strong>$120–$180</strong> for an initial inspection/diagnostic visit. RepairPal's 2021 S60 brake-system inspection estimate is $122–$179 before tax and fees. Further diagnosis or repairs are additional. See <a href="https://repairpal.com/estimator/volvo/s60/2021/brake-system-inspect-cost">RepairPal's 2021 S60 brake inspection estimate</a>.</p>

</BaseLayout>
